(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ac-13"] = {"468385101":[["","As dusk falls, campfires gradually ignite in the forest, casting orange-red shadows on the green leaves. People are bustling around, shouting constantly."],["","Hey! Put all the weapons and equipment in the temporary warehouse, and bring the food over here!"],["","Tch—damn, this thing's heavy. Someone give me a hand!"],["","Coming, coming—heave! Whoa... that's a lot of supplies. Nice, this should give everyone a breather. Where are Field and the others?"],["","They're still delivering supplies with the escort team. I heard there are a few more trucks on the way."],["","Really?! That's great! Now we can definitely hold out until we reach our destination!"],["Boy","L-Let go! Let go, Uncle Harlin!"],["","Hey Daniel, you eaten yet? Stop running around, or your pop's gonna be mad when he gets back!"],["Boy","Yeah, I had dinner... and I'm not running around! I'm about to deliver food to the patients!"],["","Daniel runs off with the tray without looking back."],["Boy","Keep it up, guys! I'm gonna head off now!"],["","Tray in hand, Daniel arrives at a row of tents, where patients lie resting on makeshift beds."],["","It's quiet here, the silence broken only by intermittent moans of pain."],["","Daniel gently places the tray on the ground and pushes it toward a crouching figure."],["Boy","Are you feeling better today, Uncle Gutzman?"],["","A dark, bony hand slips out from under the blanket he's wrapped in, snatches up a piece of dry bread, and draws back inside."],["","Anyone follow you?"],["","A man's voice, weak and short of breath, so hoarse it sounds coated in grit."],["Boy","It's okay, Uncle Gutzman. Nobody here's going to hurt you—"],["","It's noisy out there. Strangers?"],["Boy","Did you forget? I told you yesterday that supplies were being delivered today. Everyone's busy unloading them, so it's a bit loud... So don't worry, Uncle Gutzman."],["","..."],["","\"Gutzman\" eats his bread in silence."],["","Daniel's eyes dart around. Then he carefully leans down and slowly peeks through the gap in the blanket."],["Boy","!?"],["","Daniel freezes. Although he's mentally prepared himself, he's still a bit startled at the sight of that gaunt, blood-covered face."],["","What you starin' at? Careful, or I'll eat you too, kid."],["Boy","You really should eat more, Uncle Gutzman, or you'll die."],["","...I don't need no kid telling me what to do."],["Boy","I'm serious, Uncle Gutzman. Before... before Uncle Barry died, he was thin too. He couldn't eat much at all."],["","\"Gutzman's\" gaze flickers a few times as he stuffs the bread into his mouth more forcefully."],["","I won't die, kid. Still got a lot to do—"],["Boy","Y-You remember everything now, Uncle Gutzman?!"],["","......"],["","\"Gutzman\" looks away."],["","Nope. Not a thing."],["Boy","...I-It's okay! As long as you're alive, that's all that matters, Uncle Gutzman."],["Boy","When I found you, you were trapped under the rocks. You couldn't even speak, just stare at me and wheeze... I was so scared."],["","\"Gutzman\" chews in silence. The moment Daniel finishes speaking, a glint of something flashes in his vacant stare."],["","Back then... Did I say anything?"],["Boy","Nope, you were too weak to talk by then. But after we brought you back, you started rambling all kinds of nonsense. You had a really high fever the whole time. It scared Miss Hope half to death. She said if it kept up, it'd fry your brain."],["","......"],["","\"Gutzman\" picks up another piece of bread."],["Boy","Your injuries... Miss Hope patched them up for you. Just remember not to do anything too strenuous for a while..."],["","Daniel chatters on a little longer, but the look in \"Gutzman's\" eyes never changes—until Daniel says three syllables, and in an instant, he goes completely still."],["Boy","\"Georgia\"—if you want to get your memory back, maybe we can start with that name."],["","...You know Georgia?"],["Boy","Haha, knew it! The moment I said that name, you reacted, Uncle Gutzman."],["Boy","I don't know her, but you kept calling out \"Gutzman\" and \"Georgia\" while you were unconscious. I think if you put Georgia and your own name together in such a dangerous situation, that person must be very important to you, right?"],["","...Heh. Yeah, she's important to me, all right."],["","\"Gutzman\" finishes off every last bit of bread, then raises his cup and drains it in one go."],["Boy","Once you're feeling better, go find her. Don't worry, Uncle Gutzman—if you're still alive, you'll find your answers."],["","\"Gutzman\" stares at Daniel in silence, so intently that Daniel grows a little nervous. His eye sockets are so sunken that his eyeballs seem to bulge, as if they're about to be spat right out."],["","Kid... you're scared of me. So why'd you save me?"],["Boy","..."],["Boy","Actually, I was about to leave back then. But you just kept looking at me, Uncle. You didn't say a word, but I knew you really wanted to live. That you really wanted me to save you."],["","Hehe... Hehehe... Naive."],["","His laugh is an ugly sound, like wind rasping through tattered rags. Daniel looks at his front teeth, three of them broken off, and his spirits sink a little."],["Boy","Sankara's never really been peaceful. My dad's always out there, fighting all kinds of people... I keep thinking—what if one day, one day he gets hurt that badly too..."],["Boy","I just hope no one turns away when he looks at them for help."],["","Daniel props his face in his hands, looking wistful."],["Boy","Of course, I hope that day never comes for Dad."],["","Gutzman watches him, expressionless."],["Boy","I don't know what you used to do, Uncle, but I think the past is the past. Once you're better, go find Georgia and start a new life!"],["","...Yeah. As long as you're alive, there's always another chance to start over."],["","Gutzman sets the cup back down on the tray."],["","I'll be out of here tonight, kid."],["Boy","Huh? That soon? Aren't you going to wait until you're fully healed—"],["","You'll be reaching the new base soon, won't you?"],["Boy","Yeah! Dad says once we get there, life won't be so hard for everyone anymore. We won't go hungry, and there'll be more people to protect us... Still, I liked Sankara better the way it was. It's that explosion's fault we all had to leave."],["","Then tonight's the perfect time."],["Boy","...Uncle?"],["","Daniel looks a bit confused."],["","Off you go. Your dad and the others are back."],["","Daniel blinks, then stands up and looks off into the distance. A transport truck is slowly rolling toward them through a billowing cloud of dust."],["Boy","Wait... it really is my dad! How did you know?"],["","The tires. Loud as hell."],["Boy","Oh... Heh heh, I guess we've all gotten used to it... Then I'll go wait for Dad. You get some rest, Uncle. I'll come find you later."],["","Daniel picks up the tray, turns, and dashes off out of sight."],["","\"Gutzman\" stares sharply at Daniel's distant silhouette. Under his messy hair, a transparent communicator hangs on his ear, flashing with a red light."],["Guard Member","How come it's just you? Where's Field and the rest?"],["Guard Team Member","Their truck broke down. I just sent someone to go get them. Grab a few more hands to unload the supplies. Careful, don't bang anything up."],["Guard Member","Relax, I know. Everyone's lives depend on this stuff. Heh heh, one bounce of this crate and you can tell there's good stuff inside!"],["Guard Team Member","Of course. We've run into no shortage of opportunists since we pulled up stakes. We're nearly out of ammo, so this'll plug the gap nicely."],["Guard Member","Yeah. Plenty of folks in the Guard Team got hurt, and medical supplies are tight too... Good thing we've got new allies. What they sent should keep us going a while longer, at least."],["Guard Team Member","Well, it'll all work out. Hey, did you see that beauty? It came in with the earlier convoy."],["Guard Member","Heh heh, they've got that tarp wrapped around it nice and tight. The captain and the others sure treasure it. But they can't hide it from a man of the world like me. With a frame that size, it's obviously a Ha—"],["Boy","Dad!"],["Guard Member","Haha, it's Daniel! Go say hi!"],["Boy","Dad! You're finally back! Did you bring anything cool this time?"],["Guard Team Member","Sure did, buddy. Care to inspect the goods?"],["","The boy stands on tiptoe and opens the crate in a crew member's hands. It's packed with jet-black rifles."],["Boy","Wow—I've never seen this model before!"],["Guard Team Member","Hey! No touching—not right now, anyway."],["Guard Team Member","Go grab a few more guys to help unload. Once we're done counting everything, you can take a closer look."],["Boy","Okay, Dad, I'm on it!"],["","Daniel runs off, and just as the men are about to pick up their conversation, a figure suddenly appears at the depot entrance."],["Guard Team Member","...And you are?"],["Guard Member","Ah! Gutzman! What are you doing here? Are you feeling better?"],["Guard Team Member","And this is...?"],["Guard Member","Carter, this is Gutzman. Daniel brought him back a while ago when he was out on patrol. He was badly hurt and had collapsed near our camp. You've been out on assignment these past few days, so it's no wonder you didn't know."],["","Carter looks \"Gutzman\" up and down suspiciously."],["","I came to help unload."],["","These... all go in the warehouse?"],["Guard Team Member","Ah... right, thanks, man. You can leave it—I can take it from here. You're still injured, no need to push yourself—"],["","\"Gutzman\" jumps into the truck bed with practiced ease, landing with a heavy thud."],["","Heh... All good stuff, huh—"],["Guard Team Member","..."],["Guard Team Member","Hey—did you guys ever check his background?"],["Guard Member","He says he doesn't remember much. Didn't have anything on him to prove who he is, either."],["Guard Team Member","And you're still letting him stay here? What if something happens—"],["Guard Member","When Daniel dragged him back, he was barely hanging on. The kid was terrified. In that situation, what were we supposed to say—\"let him die and stay out of it\"? That'd be a hell of a lesson to teach a kid."],["","Where do these rounds go?"],["Guard Member","Hey! Here, give them to me—I'll take them!"],["","\"Gutzman\" hands down one crate of supplies, then hefts another himself and jumps down."],["Guard Team Member","Here, I'll take that. No need to trouble yourself, Mr. Gutzman."],["","Carter takes the crate from \"Gutzman's\" hands and heads deeper into the warehouse. \"Gutzman\" watches him move, quick and efficient, then slowly follows."],["","You're nothing like your kid..."],["","Carter glances back at him."],["Guard Team Member","No, we're not much alike. Daniel's been like that since he was little—always wanting to protect everyone, hoping no one gets hurt... but there are too many bad people in this world. That hope is bound to fail."],["Guard Team Member","I've always taught him to stay on guard, no matter where he is. But he believes that if everyone keeps their guard up, people will never truly understand each other... and we'll only drift further apart."],["","He's naïve, for sure... But he saved my life."],["","Carter finishes stacking the crates. When he turns back around, his expression is grave."],["Guard Team Member","He did. Which is why, Mr. Gutzman, I'd like to ask you to leave as soon as possible."],["","..."],["Guard Team Member","There's the smell of smoke and blood on you. And that kind of thing... could bring disaster to all of us."],["Guard Team Member","As you can see, we're in a pretty bad situation. The contamination from that explosion forced us to abandon the settlement we'd lived in for years and head somewhere unknown."],["Guard Team Member","A lot of people are on edge. Some are genuinely losing hope. I know I'm not the only one who feels something's off about you—but everyone's exhausted. No one has the strength left to decide whether you should stay or go. They just followed their instincts and saved you."],["Guard Team Member","But that's where it ends, Mr. Gutzman. Whoever you are, whatever you want—we saved your life, and we don't expect anything in return. Just leave as soon as you can. That alone would be the best outcome for us."],["","...Don't worry, I'll be leaving tonight."],["Guard Team Member","Is that so? Thank you very much for your understanding, Mr. Gutzman. If you..."],["","Dad! Something's wrong! Uncle Gil said there's a squad of mercs outside!"],["","The boy bursts in like a shot, panting hard."],["Guard Team Member","Daniel? What did you say?!"],["","Someone rushes out from the depot."],["Guard Member","What?! Damn it—those vultures just won't quit!"],["Guard Member","I'll go check it out. You stay here and watch the depot—"],["Guard Team Member","Okay, be careful!"],["Boy","Dad... everyone's going to be okay, right?"],["Guard Team Member","It's okay. The captain and the others are there. They can handle it."],["Boy","Are you going over there? I can stay here and guard the depot."],["Guard Team Member","No, Daniel. Take Hope and the others somewhere safe."],["Boy","Okay, Dad. I'll get everyone—wait...? Uncle Gutzman! What are you doing here?"],["","Gutzman is silent for two seconds."],["","...Daniel."],["Boy","Yes?"],["","It's the first time Uncle Gutzman has called him by name."],["","You people living such hard lives on Milkhama... that in itself is a sin."],["Guard Team Member","What do you mean—"],["","No one here makes allowances for the weak. If you choose to stay—whether by choice or not—you'd better be ready to face death."],["","Anyone living in Milkhama has to understand that..."],["","Otherwise, when that day comes without warning, you won't even know how to face it. Right?"],["","Carter freezes. Confusion flickers through his mind for an instant, but his body has already sensed something, and his hand reaches for his hip of its own accord."],["Boy","Uncle Gutzman, what are you—"],["","His son's voice rings in Carter's ears—but in the same moment, he sees \"Gutzman\" pull a pistol from beneath his clothes."],["Guard Team Member","!?"],["","It all happens impossibly fast—or perhaps impossibly slow. Carter instinctively turns and throws himself over Daniel. In that instant, he hears a gunshot, and a searing, tearing pain rips through his whole back."],["Boy","Dad?! Dad, what's wrong?! Da—ah!"],["","Bang, bang—! \"Gutzman\" steps closer and fires several more shots."],["","................"],["","..."],["","......"],["","\"Gutzman\" stares unblinkingly at Daniel, clutched in Carter's arms. The boy's trembling eyes are full of terror."],["","Gutzman pauses as noise comes through his headset. He places his index finger on the trigger again—gently curling it—"],["","Click—a short, crisp metallic clink, but no bullet fires."],["","Out of ammo."],["","Gutzman's eyes never leave Daniel's face, but his hand smoothly fishes a magazine out of his pocket. He sees Carter's blood welling from the wounds; some of it spattered onto Daniel's pale face when Carter threw himself down."],["","The boy never once looks away from him."],["","\"If one day my dad got hurt that badly too... I'd hope people wouldn't ignore the look in his eyes, begging for help.\""],["","......"],["???","Hey, Douglas! Can you speed it up over there?! Those guys are calling for backup. If they get here, things are gonna go south for us fast!"],["Douglas","......"],["","Douglas silently changes direction and walks slowly into the depths of the warehouse. Only when Daniel's face is completely hidden from view does he finally look away."],["Douglas","Got it. I'm done on my end. I can pull out with the supplies right now. Get ready to rendezvous with me."],["???","That's great! Can't believe your little trick actually worked. Hahahaha! Bet those Harpy guys never figured you'd live to see this day, huh?"],["","Douglas's footsteps gradually fade away. Daniel begins to tremble faintly, tears of terror pouring uncontrollably from his eyes."],["Guard Team Member","Don't... make a sound, kid... don't... make a sound..."],["","Daniel squeezes his eyes shut—he can't make a sound, because his father's hand is clamped tightly over his mouth."],["Guard Team Member","You have to... live on... Daniel... My... son... Live on... live... live..."],["","A faint whimper escapes Daniel's throat. He clings desperately to the front of his father's shirt and feels his hands turn slick and sticky."],["","Vesper Base."],["Vesper Warrior","Hey, shift change, man."],["Vesper Warrior","Hmm? Why are you back? Weren't you out with Captain Cassha and the others?"],["Vesper Warrior","We were just going over to Sankara to check the situation. Didn't need that many people, so Captain Arthur brought us back."],["Vesper Warrior","Makes sense. Plenty of those Milkhamans are hostile to us. If too many of us showed up, they'd probably think we were looking for trouble, huh?"],["Vesper Warrior","I really don't get why the captains rushed over there the minute they heard about the attack. We can barely look after ourselves right now..."],["Vesper Warrior","The captains are just worried it's some new League scheme. The Milkhamans can only do so much to protect themselves. Are we supposed to just sit back and do nothing?"],["Vesper Warrior","Why not? The most important thing for us right now is getting revenge on Lukmund. Once we've dealt with the DLAF for good, who's going to hurt them then?"],["","His voice gradually drops, and a glint of resentment creeps into his eyes."],["Vesper Warrior","Besides, haven't you ever had your doubts about those people? They'd love nothing more than to see us wiped out. Who's to say they didn't secretly team up with Lukmund and get Phoenix killed?"],["Vesper Warrior","..."],["Vesper Warrior","...Hey, stop complaining, Dasko. If Captain Arthur hears you, you'll definitely get punched."],["Vesper Warrior","I'm not the only one who thinks this way. The other guys are saying it too! Phoenix died under mysterious circumstances, and we need to avenge him! What are we doing cowering here?"],["Vesper Warrior","Why aren't we moving yet? When are we going to kill that bastard Lukmund? What are we waiting for?!"],["","For my fist."],["","Thud. Dasko takes a punch, his footing slipping as he drops to one knee."],["Vesper Warrior","Captain Arthur?!"],["Arthur","Shouldn't you be on duty? What's all this chatter?"],["Vesper Warrior","I..."],["Vesper Warrior","...Nothing, Captain Arthur. It's shift change—we were just going over the handoff."],["","Arthur looks at the two of them. Dasko never makes eye contact with Arthur, his lips pressed tightly together."],["Arthur","Got it. Switch out. I'll take a look here."],["Vesper Warrior","Yes, sir. I'll be off then."],["","Dasko quickly finishes speaking and jogs straight out of the post."],["Vesper Warrior","...You heard all of that, didn't you?"],["","Arthur glances at her silently without responding."],["Vesper Warrior","Haha... honestly, you hear that kind of talk everywhere these days. Even if it's not here, you'll hear it somewhere else."],["Arthur","What about you, Selena? What do you think?"],["Vesper Warrior","My opinion doesn't really matter. I follow the captains' lead."],["","Selena smiles."],["Arthur","..."],["Arthur","Phoenix's... passing... it's something everyone carries. I understand how they feel."],["Arthur","But because of that, we have to carry on his will—keep moving forward, and not let hatred blind us into throwing our lives away for nothing."],["","Arthur's gaze drifts past the layered clouds, as if searching for something far beyond."],["Vesper Warrior","Captain, now that we've come this far, it's hard to say everyone is still moving toward the same goal. All the fighting has turned everyone... a little twisted?"],["Vesper Warrior","After going through those things, everyone needs an outlet for release."],["Arthur","But on Milkhama, can anyone truly do as they please? Can anyone really find an outlet just because they want one?"],["Arthur","Even if we find that exit, will things really get better because of it?"],["Vesper Warrior","...Sorry, Captain, I didn't mean to put you in a difficult position."],["Arthur","I know you're just stating the facts... But precisely because of that, we must stay rational and avoid making decisions that could make things worse."],["","A flash catches Arthur's attention, and she shifts her gaze slightly back."],["Arthur","Wait, Selena—get in your ST. Get ready."],["Vesper Warrior","Captain? Is there a situation?!"],["","Arthur raises her tactical binoculars and looks toward the flash, then pulls out her communicator and tunes it to the live channel."],["Arthur","Deliberately trying to get my attention... So, what exactly is your purpose?"],["","Arthur Nadib?"],["Arthur","You are..."],["","Arthur feels a bit bewildered, but the voice is very familiar—a name is on the tip of her tongue."],["","Thunderbolt Squad, Mirestomp."],["","Through the binoculars, Arthur watches a Dias stand up, its pilot's hatch wide open, and she can clearly see a familiar figure squinting and smiling at the edge of the hatch."],["Arthur","Snow Kratt..."],["Mirestomp","Long time no see, \"Captain\" Arthur."],["Arthur","Why are you here?"],["Mirestomp","I recently heard some interesting news related to you guys, so of course I had to come and verify it."],["Arthur","Verify?"],["Mirestomp","Where's Captain Cassha? Not here?"],["Arthur","Stop beating around the bush, Snow. What exactly do you want?"],["Mirestomp","Surrounded on all sides, nowhere left to run... Vesper really is in a sorry state these days."],["","Arthur grits her teeth."],["Arthur","That's not for an exile like you to mock—did you come all this way just to run your mouth?"],["Mirestomp","......"],["Mirestomp","I'm just curious—why refuse that offer of cooperation...? After all..."],["Mirestomp","Mr. Yevgeny would at least provide strong support."],["","Arthur pauses, then quickly catches on."],["Arthur","So Goman still hasn't given up? Sending you as a negotiator now?"],["Mirestomp","Do I really look like his messenger? No, no. Like I said, I'm just here to confirm a few things that interest me."],["Arthur","Stay away from us. We don't welcome anyone with ulterior motives snooping around—"],["Mirestomp","Where's Captain Cassha? At this point, don't tell me you're still planning to split up and stir up trouble."],["Arthur","That's none of your concern, Snow Kratt. Since you're so eager to cause trouble, I don't mind teaching you a lesson."],["Arthur","Assault team—surround her!"]],"468385401":[["Mirestomp","...Ah. So you're not in the mood to have a proper conversation."],["Arthur","Hmph. If you're here on Goman's behalf, then I haven't forgotten what he did to us."],["Arthur","He offered cooperation, got rejected, then stirred up the Milkhama locals to attack us, and even tried to take our wounded. Someone like that will never be an ally."],["Mirestomp","And now that you've lost most of your \"allies,\" what makes you think you can keep moving forward?"],["Arthur","That still doesn't mean we bow to Goman. Honestly... I'm disappointed, Snow. So you really did come for him, rushing all the way here just to push us into the fire."],["Mirestomp","......"],["Mirestomp","..."],["Mirestomp","Heh."],["Mirestomp","Of course, I am no longer a member of Vesper. Now my code name is only \"Mirestomp.\""],["Mirestomp","Captain Arthur, after everything that's happened, isn't it a little naive of you to still cling to fantasies about me?"],["Arthur","You—"],["Mirestomp","Alright, I was just passing by. Now that we've caught up, I should be leaving."],["","Dias stows its weapons and swiftly falls back under cover."],["Vesper Warrior","Captain! She's withdrawing. Should we pursue?"],["Arthur","No, it might be a misdirection—we just need to guard the stronghold and wait for Cassha and the others to return."],["Vesper Warrior","Understood. Our stronghold is so remote, I really don't know how she managed to get here—but it certainly couldn't have been \"just passing by.\""],["Arthur","......"],["Arthur","Snow Kratt, what are you really after?"]],"468389101":[["Black Market Merchant","Here's the final bill. The surplus has gone back into your usual account. Take a look."],["","Mirestomp swipes the terminal screen, confirms the bill is correct, and signs her codename at the bottom."],["Mirestomp","Long time no see. Your operation's looking more legit by the day, old dog."],["Black Market Merchant","Haha, business is tough, Miss Mirestomp. Everyone wants to keep all the profit for themselves, but where in the world do you find a deal like that?"],["Black Market Merchant","All we can do is make sure every exchange along the way is fair, and let our customers see they're not being cheated."],["Mirestomp","Wise words. Sounds like you've had some trouble lately."],["Black Market Merchant","It's all behind me now, Miss Mirestomp. Just look around my shop—you'll see it was all worth it."],["","Mirestomp's gaze sweeps lightly over the shop. It looks less like an ST repair shop and more like a small testing facility."],["","Since they first met, the old dog has made quite a name for himself."],["Black Market Merchant","Did something happen, Miss Mirestomp? I haven't seen Dias this badly damaged in a long time."],["Mirestomp","......"],["","Mirestomp remains silent, glancing at the old dog with a faint smile."],["Black Market Merchant","...Understood. I spoke out of turn."],["Black Market Merchant","Well then, pleasure doing business, Miss Mirestomp. Your ST's been repaired and is ready for pickup."],["Mirestomp","Thank you."],["","Mirestomp turns to leave, scrolling through the messages on her terminal as she walks."],["","In the days since she left, a stack of unread messages has piled up: Skysweep, Blazetrudge, Grimbite..."],["","At first, they only asked where she was. In the end, they all went quiet."],["","Mirestomp's fingertip hovers over Grimbite's codename. After a few seconds' hesitation, she puts the terminal back in her pocket."],["","Suddenly, her nose twitches. She glances sideways into the darkness behind her and lets out a soft laugh."],["Mirestomp","Think you covered your tracks pretty well, huh? Tailing me all this way must've been exhausting. Why don't you come out so we can talk?"],["","Mirestomp walks slowly over to Dias, which rests on one knee. There's no one around her—no one she could be talking to."],["","She steps onto the rope ladder but doesn't climb straight up to the cockpit. Instead, she gazes casually across the hangar. Several STs are parked there, and only a few staff members move back and forth among them."],["Mirestomp","I know you can hear me, just like I can always feel your eyes on me... How about I guess who you are?"],["Mirestomp","You've been following me for this long, so you must be very interested in what I'm up to. You can't have missed the markers I left along the way—but you didn't understand them, so you kept following me, and that's how I noticed you here..."],["Mirestomp","Which means you're not my ally."],["Mirestomp","You've had plenty of chances to attack me along the way, but you've kept quiet—so I'll go out on a limb and guess you're not my enemy either..."],["","Mirestomp's smile gives away nothing of her mood."],["Mirestomp","So... Predator. Why have you been following me ever since you left the outpost?"],["","......"],["","In an instant, even the staff seem to have melted away, leaving nothing but an unbroken silence."],["","Kzzzt—kzzzt—"],["","Dias's communication interface lights up, and Mirestomp hears a voice from above."],["","I'm not surprised you noticed—"],["","Mirestomp scales the rope ladder, slips back into the cockpit, and quickly traces the transmission's source."],["","You're the color of snow, Miss Mirestomp... I knew you would sense me sooner or later. Against snow, every anomaly glares."],["","Mirestomp quickly searches her memory for this voice, and soon her lips curl in recognition."],["Mirestomp","It's you... Libby."],["","A faint tremor runs through the ground as a glow emerges from among the rows of STs."],["Libby","Yes, Miss Mirestomp. We have never spoken at length, but knowing you has still been a great—"],["Mirestomp","Did your president send you to follow me?"],["","Mirestomp cuts her off."],["","Mirestomp keeps smiling as usual—yet something has definitely changed."],["Libby","No. I am acting on my own judgment, Miss Mirestomp."],["Mirestomp","Hmm, hmm... So by your judgment, I'm a threat to you."],["Libby","I cannot trust what is merely assumed. I choose to see for myself."],["Mirestomp","And? Has your view of me changed?"],["Libby","..."],["Libby","I cannot comprehend your actions, Miss Mirestomp. From what I have observed, your only aim on this trip seems to be reaching some kind of agreement with Vesper."],["","Mirestomp's smile falters slightly."],["Libby","Yet your resolve seems weak. You were ready to withdraw after a single failure."],["Mirestomp","......"],["Libby","Was that a feint? Perhaps your visit has a purpose I have not yet noticed..."],["Mirestomp","Being second-guessed by a heartless freak like you... It's quite a peculiar feeling."],["Libby","......"],["Libby","In fact, the world looks different to everyone. Everyone is an outlier in someone's eyes, Miss Mirestomp."],["Libby","To me, you are like snow, and I am trying to understand everything about you. That is the foundation of our future cooperation, is it not?"],["Mirestomp","Fine words... Hah. You're just clearing every risk out of your boss's way... He's got something big going on lately, hasn't he?"],["Libby","...I will not deny it. It is, after all, my duty."],["Libby","Well then, Miss Mirestomp, if you're willing, perhaps we could—"],["Mirestomp","No."],["","Mirestomp shoots back without missing a beat, her smile growing even wider."],["Mirestomp","Lucky for you, I'm in a good mood today."],["Mirestomp","So I'm going to teach you, very carefully, how to behave around me—and we'll start with you not tailing me whenever you feel like it."],["","Dias's optics flash as it straightens up."]],"468389301":[["","Aglow staggers helplessly back several steps until it slams into the hangar wall, leaving a dent."],["","It has nowhere left to go, and Dias's gun is already trained on its cockpit."],["Mirestomp","Last warning—stop trying to figure me out, Libby, or all you'll get is a bullet. Got it?"],["Libby","......"],["Libby","A record of this battle will reach headquarters the moment I die, and everyone will know it was you who killed me, Miss Mirestomp."],["Mirestomp","Is that a threat?"],["Libby","No. Merely a friendly reminder. I know your current employer values his partnership with the president. You would not want to disappoint him, would you?"],["Mirestomp","...Heh."],["Mirestomp","But if he found out your president and his lackeys don't put much trust in this partnership, maybe he'd reconsider whether to keep it going?"],["Libby","..."],["","Libby lets out a faint sigh."],["Libby","Miss Mirestomp, we may belong to different factions, but I believe we both have the loyalty expected of us."],["Libby","I don't intend to interfere with your actions. But a secret Thunderbolt Squad deployment in peacetime is suspicious enough that I cannot turn a blind eye."],["Mirestomp","I am not acting as a member of the Thunderbolt Squad—"],["Libby","Then what about Mr. Blazetrudge?"],["Mirestomp","—What?"],["Libby","The two of you left the base at almost the same time. That inevitably raises questions about your intentions."],["","Mirestomp frowns, recalling the last message Blazetrudge sent her—\"Mirestomp, where are you?\""],["","She didn't answer it, but she knows her companions understand the meaning behind her silence."],["","..."],["","Could she have been wrong?"],["","Mirestomp quickly dials Blazetrudge's communicator, and he picks up swiftly."],["Mirestomp","Where are you?"],["Blazetrudge","......"],["Blazetrudge","—Bzzt—Blazetrudge—bzzt—in the ST."],["Mirestomp","Your coordinates? Give me your coordinates."],["Blazetrudge","Kzzzt—kzzzt—kzzzt—"],["Blazetrudge","Blazetrudge—bzzt—can't—be—bzzt—found by Mirestomp—"],["","Mirestomp presses her lips together and quickly uses the comms signal to trace Blazetrudge's coordinates. But just as she narrows it down to an area, the call cuts out."],["","..."],["","Mirestomp takes a deep breath."],["Libby","I do hope your silence means you're savoring my predicament, Miss Mirestomp."],["","Dias lowers its gun and takes a few steps back."],["Mirestomp","You've been tailing both me and Blazetrudge, haven't you?"],["Libby","Of course."],["Mirestomp","So... you tampered with the markers I left for my \"team\" too?"],["Libby","..."],["Mirestomp","When I realized someone was following me, I suspected it might be them, so I left a marker telling them I wouldn't put myself in danger. I just needed some time to deal with something personal..."],["Mirestomp","But Blazetrudge is clearly still being tracked."],["","And wherever he is now, there's a powerful source of signal interference—which fills Mirestomp with an ominous suspicion."],["Libby","Yes, Miss Mirestomp. At the time, in order to interfere with your actions, I did alter your marker to feed Mr. Blazetrudge false information."],["Libby","My honesty may anger you and put me at a disadvantage, but I trust that your priority is finding Mr. Blazetrudge."],["","Mirestomp's smile returns."],["Mirestomp","Then, Libby, I take it you're ready to tell me exactly what marker you showed Blazetrudge?"]],"468393101":[["","The convoy rumbles steadily down the old overgrown road."],["","The mercenaries belt out off-key songs, casting satisfied glances at the supplies piled high in the rear carriage."],["","In a passenger seat, Douglas keeps flicking his lighter, trying to get a cigarette lit—he's failed twice already."],["","Grip the lighter. Roll the wheel. Touch the flame to the tobacco... It should be such a simple thing."],["","But Douglas's thumb is missing its nail, and as he works the wheel, his fingers keep slipping... The flame seems to reject him."],["Mercenary","Give it here, I'll—"],["Douglas","Just drive."],["","The guy in the driver's seat looks away awkwardly."],["","On the fifth try, a faint click sounds in the cab. Douglas finally gets his cigarette lit and takes a long, deep drag."],["","Then he breaks into a violent fit of coughing."],["Mercenary","Hey, easy there, will you? If you're not feeling well, don't smoke. And don't die in my truck."],["Douglas","Cough, cough! Cough, cough—cough—you—cough, cough—shut up—cough, cough!"],["","You've really been through it, brother. I've never seen you in such bad shape. What the hell did Harpy do to you?"],["","At the mention of that all-too-familiar name, Douglas's gaze turns suddenly vicious."],["Douglas","Look at the state of me... Use your imagination."],["Mercenary","...Cough."],["","The mercenaries don't dare say a word. If Douglas walked into any mercenary hub right now, no one would recognize him. All they'd see is a skeleton in clothes, staggering around."],["","The sight would be horrifying."],["Mercenary","Your call gave me a real shock. We all thought—"],["Douglas","—I was dead, right?"],["Mercenary","Gutzman and Georgia ganged up on you and handed you over to Harpy... We could only assume the worst."],["Douglas","You weren't wrong. If it weren't for that explosion, I wouldn't be sitting here now."],["Mercenary","So what's your next move?"],["Douglas","Like I told you. Revenge."],["Douglas","Harpy, Gutzman, Georgia... All of them."],["Mercenary","Hey... About that..."],["Douglas","What, Layton? You're not thinking of backing out, are you?"],["Douglas","Look at all that loot back there. If I hadn't tipped you off, you really think you'd have gotten your hands on all that?"],["Mercenary","I haven't forgotten, but this needs careful handling. For one thing, you're not exactly in top shape right now. For another... well, you probably haven't heard, have you? Gutzman's dead."],["","Douglas's eyes widen slightly."],["Douglas","...Don't talk nonsense."],["Mercenary","I'm not lying. A lot went down out there while you were locked up."],["Mercenary","Gutzman and Georgia had a falling out and ended up teaming with Michaela. Later, they clashed again—a full-on fight—and that's how Gutzman died."],["Douglas","......"],["Douglas","..."],["Douglas","Heh... heh heh... Hahahaha—cough, cough—cough, cough, cough!"],["Mercenary","Hey, hey! Don't get worked up. Don't worry about the mess we're in. One day, brother... one day, we'll settle the score."],["","Douglas wipes his face and takes another deep drag. This time he doesn't cough. His expression eases a great deal, as if he's savoring a taste he hasn't had in a long time, and he even blows a few smoke rings."],["Douglas","Yeah... that day'll come. But damn it, that bastard didn't die by my hand..."],["Douglas","Back then, he and Georgia ganged up on me and left me with gaping wounds. When I was barely clinging to life, they handed me over to Harpy."],["","Douglas pauses. His cloudy eyes go vacant again as his mind replays the scene like a silent film."],["Douglas","Unless you've been there... Layton, you can't imagine what it's like inside Harpy... Heh. The people there are like executioners straight out of hell."],["Mercenary","Tough luck, man."],["","Layton glances at the road and mutters his agreement, as casual as ever. Douglas looks at him so intently that he forgets to take another drag."],["","\"Tough luck, man.\" All the torment he endured on the brink of death, all the despair that torment bred—in other people's eyes, it all comes down to those three throwaway words."],["","...But what right does he have to argue?"],["","He's just killed the father of the child who once saved his life, and the blood on his hands hasn't even been washed off yet. And his reason for killing the man? He was simply in the way of Douglas's fortune. Tough luck that it happened to be then."],["","And Douglas? All the pain he suffered was simply because he was in the way of someone else's fortune. Tough luck that it happened to be him..."],["Douglas","Heh heh... heh heh heh..."],["Mercenary","What're you thinking about?"],["","Douglas snaps back to reality, noticing a bit of ash has fallen on his thigh. He gently blows it away, takes one last drag of his cigarette, and flicks the butt out the window."],["Douglas","Nothing, Layton. This world's just full of shit..."],["Douglas","We need to pull off something big, Layton, right now, something big."],["Mercenary","Huh? Wasn't what we just did big enough?"],["Douglas","Not even close! A refugee camp? How's that supposed to be enough?"],["Douglas","Somebody's backing those refugees. Once they find out the camp got raided, they'll send people after us for sure."],["Mercenary","Oh man, why didn't you say so earlier?! We need to keep a low profile for a while—"],["Douglas","Don't be so naive! Think about that big piece of hardware... Hades. What kind of faction lets just anyone walk off with something like that?!"],["Mercenary","...Yeah..."],["Douglas","We can lie low for a while, but not forever—unless you're planning to leave that thing in the warehouse collecting dust!"],["Mercenary","So what's the plan?"],["Douglas","...Vesper."],["Mercenary","Huh?!"],["Douglas","I heard from the refugees that Vesper's base is nearby."],["Mercenary","No way... You're seriously thinking of hitting a real army's base?!"],["Douglas","They're not the Vesper they used to be. Phoenix is dead, and the DLAF's been hunting down what's left of them. They're a spent force. We've got a real shot at taking them down now!"],["Mercenary","..."],["","Layton's eyes go wide, and for a moment he's at a loss for words. Douglas's eyes burn with obsession; he isn't going to hear a single objection."],["Douglas","Trust me, you don't want to end up being hunted, and you can't imagine what's waiting for you if those executioners get their hands on you—Layton, we need to build up our strength!"],["Mercenary","Uh... can it... really be done?"],["Douglas","Luck can't always be on your side, and the more you crave success, the more you have to create opportunities for yourself—even if it means risking your life."],["Mercenary","Sss... Oh, man..."],["Douglas","Vesper's been getting support from Harpy too, and they definitely have some valuable stuff. Take them out, and all that loot is ours!"],["","Layton scratches his head awkwardly, trying to think of a way to say no. But out of the corner of his eye, he catches Douglas making a dangerous move—reaching for something on his side of the cab."],["","Layton swerves sharply, the truck drifting fast. Douglas, caught off guard, slams into the window, and the gun he's just grabbed clatters to the floor."],["","Before Douglas can react, Layton suddenly shouts."],["Mercenary","Wait! Douglas, there's something ahead!"],["","Douglas hooks his rifle with his foot and drags it back, then calmly pulls out his tactical binoculars. It doesn't take long for the silhouettes of several mechs to appear in his lenses."],["Mercenary","What is that?"],["Douglas","...Not sure. At this distance, they've definitely spotted us. Put everyone on alert—we've got the numbers, so a little skirmish won't scare us."],["","The truck speeds up, and Douglas's group is soon closing in on the ST squad that appeared out of nowhere."],["","Before they can hail them, a Mithril approaches them first."],["Blazetrudge","Mirestomp. Blazetrudge... has been waiting for you."],["Douglas","...Who are you?"],["Blazetrudge","Not... Mirestomp?"],["","Douglas frowns. The name sounds vaguely familiar."],["Mercenary","Ah! Thunderbolt Squad! Mirestomp—she's with the Thunderbolt Squad!"],["Blazetrudge","...?"],["Blazetrudge","Do you know... where Mirestomp is?"],["Blazetrudge","Mirestomp is in danger... Blazetrudge has to help..."],["Mercenary","Who knows? Isn't your Thunderbolt Squad always impossible to pin down?"],["Blazetrudge","Blazetrudge... doesn't understand... Where is Mirestomp?"],["Douglas","...Forget it. Don't waste time on him. Let's go."],["","With the alarm lifted, Layton doesn't give it much more thought. After all, they really do have the numbers and the firepower now..."],["","Just as the engine roars back to life, Douglas hears a series of explosions—"],["","He whips around on instinct to see a line of transport trucks blown to pieces, roaring flames belching thick black smoke."],["","Mithril, with Blazetrudge at the controls, is still frozen in a bizarre knife-throwing pose that looks incredibly clumsy."],["Blazetrudge","Blade... hard to use..."],["Blazetrudge","Blazetrudge... still has to protect Mirestomp..."],["Mercenary","Damn it..."],["","Douglas stares at the fire behind the truck, his jaw trembling."],["Blazetrudge","Mirestomp... where are you...?"],["Douglas","Crush him—!"]],"468393301":[["","Under the relentless barrage, Blazetrudge maneuvers Mithril, only just dodging the attacks."],["","He has no chance of winning this fight, but he still clings to his convictions."],["Blazetrudge","Mirestomp... Blazetrudge... must protect Mirestomp..."],["","—beep beep beep—"],["","The comms interface suddenly lights up. Blazetrudge glances at it, touches his mask uneasily, and accepts the call."],["Mirestomp","—Bzzt—bzzt—Where—"],["Blazetrudge","......"],["Blazetrudge","Blazetrudge... here, in the ST..."],["Mirestomp","—Bzzt—coordinates—bzzt—your—bzzt—"],["","Blazetrudge takes a deep breath, remembers what Grimbite told him before he set out, and answers earnestly."],["Blazetrudge","Blazetrudge... can't be... found by Mirestomp—"],["","Whoosh! A missile tears through the cover behind Mithril, and Blazetrudge feels a violent jolt. The comms interface dissolves into static and goes dark after barely two seconds."],["Blazetrudge","Mirestomp... in danger..."],["Blazetrudge","Blazetrudge... protect Mirestomp..."],["","But Mirestomp's voice doesn't come back. Blazetrudge stares at the screen for two seconds—and before he can react, an ST has crept up behind him."],["Douglas","Die, you bastard—!"],["","Mithril's optics flash as it swings its blade even faster, cleanly slicing off the right arm of Douglas's ST."],["Douglas","Damn it! Surround him—surround him!"],["","Mithril surges forward, cutting down every ST that tries to block it with a single slash. In the end, all anyone can do is watch helplessly as it shrinks into the distance."],["Douglas","After him! He's going to pay for this... After him!"],["Mercenary","Douglas! Calm down! He's not worth chasing all over the place!"],["","Layton brings his ST up alongside Douglas's. In the cockpit, Douglas is breathing hard and doesn't answer."],["Mercenary","Come on, let's get out of here."],["Douglas","......"],["","Layton feels a rush of relief, thinking they can just leave it at that. But in an instant, Douglas pulls the trigger, and bullets rain down on Layton's ST—"],["Mercenary","Doug... las... you—!"],["","Boom—!! Layton's ST explodes."],["Douglas","Go wait it out in hell, Layton..."],["","He moves past the wreckage of Layton's ST and presses on. Not far ahead sit several trucks, loaded with the spoils of their journey—and enough manpower."],["","Now it will all be his."],["","Dias and Aglow both kneel, their cockpits wide open. Their pilots stand at their feet."],["","Mirestomp scoops up a small handful of soil, feeling how warm it is."],["Mirestomp","The fighting here ended not long ago."],["Libby","There's still a strong smell of gunpowder..."],["","Mirestomp stands up, her gaze following the chaotic tracks on the ground into the distance."],["Mirestomp","You changed my marker and made Blazetrudge think I was in danger, so he waited here to back me up... and ran into an enemy instead."],["Libby","There was a reason for it, Miss Mirestomp. I didn't set you up on purpose. Besides, Mr. Blazetrudge's body isn't here, so there's a good chance he's still alive."],["Mirestomp","......"],["","Mirestomp glances aside. Not far off, human remains lie scattered among the ST debris, blown apart so thoroughly that the fighting here must have been extremely fierce."],["","She also recognizes a few familiar scraps of fabric. They might have belonged to the people who came out with Blazetrudge to look for her."],["Libby","We're quite close to Sankara and the Vesper base here. If we want to find Mr. Blazetrudge quickly, we could try—"],["Mirestomp","I know where he might go."],["Libby","Yes?"],["Mirestomp","Heavy fighting can make Blazetrudge lose his head. He gets agitated and insecure, and this place used to be his..."],["","Home."],["Mirestomp","...He might follow his old memories back there."],["","Mirestomp steps onto the rope ladder and climbs back into her ST."],["Mirestomp","Let's move. This lead's worth chasing, whatever it takes."]],"468397101":[["Vesper Warrior","We should leave now, Captain."],["Cassha","......"],["","The sky is overcast, with only the ruined camp still burning in the distance. Cassha stares at the blaze, her eyes tinged with a hint of weary sorrow."],["Cassha","Is the team all set?"],["Vesper Warrior","Yes, Captain."],["Vesper Warrior","...We all think you were hard done by this time. Everyone's pissed."],["Cassha","Hard done by? Heh, you mean being held at gunpoint and yelled at by those Milkhamans?"],["Vesper Warrior","I just don't get it, Captain—you came here to save them! They were robbed, attacked and hurt... yet all they do is blame Vesper!"],["Vesper Warrior","But we didn't do anything wrong..."],["Cassha","It's okay, Gina. They were just venting their frustration. They didn't actually lay a hand on me, after all."],["Vesper Warrior","You shouldn't have to stand there and take their abuse! I won't stand for it!"],["Cassha","Heh, that's quite the scowl..."],["","Chuckling, Cassha walks past Gina and over to her ST."],["Cassha","Try not to frown so much. You're still young. Don't want premature wrinkles now, do we?"],["Vesper Warrior","Captain! How can you make fun of me at a time like this..."],["Cassha","As long as we confirm that this attack has no connection with the DL side, our goal will be achieved. Gina, you don't need to worry about anything else."],["","Cassha steps onto the rope ladder and is slowly pulled back into the cockpit."],["Cassha","Go back. There are more important things to—"],["","Her voice falters, as if she's caught sight of something and her mind is drawn elsewhere."],["Vesper Warrior","Captain? Is something wrong?"],["Cassha","...No, I must have been mistaken."],["Cassha","Let's go. We're heading home."],["Arthur","Cassha, are you already on your way back?"],["Cassha","Yes. Why are you contacting me now? Did something happen?"],["Arthur","...Actually, it's not a big deal. I just wanted to remind you to be careful on your way back. Mirestomp came by while you were away."],["Cassha","Snow? What did she want?"],["Arthur","Who knows? She just came by and started talking weird. Seems she's on some mission for Goman."],["Cassha","Got it. You take care of this place. I'll be back soon."],["Arthur","Stay safe, Cassha."],["Cassha","Don't worry, we—"],["Vesper Warrior","Captain, there's an ST approaching us up ahead!"],["Arthur","What happened?"],["Cassha","It's okay. I can handle it. See you later, Arthur."],["","Cassha quickly ends the call."],["Cassha","Let's go check."],["","Cassha zooms in on the display—a heavily damaged Mithril, its hull throwing off sparks as it moves. It doesn't look like much of a threat."],["Vesper Warrior","Stop! Identify yourself!"],["","The Mithril slowly comes to a stop, stubbornly raising its blade with a labored, clanking movement."],["Blazetrudge","Blazetrudge... protect Mirestomp..."],["Blazetrudge","Mirestomp... where..."],["Blazetrudge","Danger... danger... Blazetrudge, burn everyone..."],["Vesper Warrior","Mirestomp and Blazetrudge?"],["Vesper Warrior","Captain, it's the Thunderbolt Squad!"],["","Cassha frowns. How could it be such a coincidence that both of them are in this area at the same time?"],["Vesper Warrior","Should we get rid of him, Captain? He's alone. It won't be much trouble."],["Cassha","No need, we—"],["","Before Cassha can finish speaking, a high-speed round shoots toward the Mithril from behind them. The Mithril can't dodge in time, and the round tears through what's left of its arm joint, severing the limb entirely."],["Cassha","Who fired without my order?"],["Vesper Warrior","N-no, Captain, there are other enemies—"],["","Cassha turns her ST around, only to see an aging Aker aiming its gun straight at them, smoke still drifting up from its muzzle."],["Cassha","You are..."],["Boy","C-Captain Cassha, let me help you—"],["Cassha","You are... Sankara's..."],["","The Aker puts away its gun and slowly approaches them."],["Boy","My name is Daniel. I mean no harm—Captain Cassha, please, let me join Vesper."],["","Cassha is taken aback. Daniel has already initiated a video call, and on the screen, the child's face is clear and desperate."],["Arthur","......"],["Cassha","......"],["Boy","I promise I'll be the best you've got. I won't let you down, Captain Cassha. Please, just let me join Vesper."],["Cassha","......"],["Arthur","Hey, kiddo, do you know what you should really be doing right now?"],["","Arthur glances at the time displayed on the desk."],["Arthur","Go get yourself some dinner and get a good night's sleep. Wouldn't want to miss out on growing taller, would you?"],["Boy","Don't underestimate me. I just shot that big guy. Isn't that enough to prove my strength?!"],["Arthur","Vesper's full of people who can do that. You—"],["Cassha","Arthur."],["Arthur","...Yes, Miss Cassha."],["","Arthur shrugs and silently walks to the side."],["Cassha","Daniel, right?"],["Boy","Yes, Captain."],["Cassha","I'm not your captain, you can call me Cassha."],["Boy","Cassha..."],["Cassha","Hehe, you're quite sensible."],["","Cassha smiles and ruffles Daniel's hair."],["Cassha","So that shadow I saw when we were leaving the base... that was you running after us, right?"],["Boy","...Yes."],["Cassha","Not bad... you even managed to fool my eyes. I guess you're barely passing."],["Boy","Really?! Cassha, I can join Vesper?!"],["Cassha","Yes, Daniel, you can."],["Arthur","Cassha—"],["","Cassha shakes her head at Arthur."],["Boy","Awesome, so awesome... So, um, can I go out on missions right away? Do I get my own ST and weapons? Who will I be—"],["Cassha","You are the youngest warrior in all of Vesper, Daniel. I will assign you a special mission."],["Boy","What?"],["Cassha","Guard the most important base for us—the place where the Milkhamans are about to settle."],["Boy","...?"],["Boy","...Are you... are you sending me away, Cassha?"],["Cassha","Of course not. This is a really important mission. Entrusting it to you is my way of showing trust."],["Boy","B-but I really want to go with you! Let me stay! I can definitely help!"],["Arthur","Hey, kid. You didn't screw up at home and run off, did you?"],["Arthur","Come on, be honest. Why do you want to join us so badly?"],["Boy","Nothing like that! I just really... really want to join Vesper. I hate the DL. I want to drive them all out of our home! I... I..."],["Cassha","Alright, alright, Daniel."],["","Cassha crouches down to meet Daniel at eye level."],["Cassha","I understand your hatred, your anger. But right now, we need to calm down and think about what you can do with this drive."],["Cassha","You can become a Vesper warrior anytime. Vesper warriors always fight to survive, which means we constantly think about how to use the life we have to create the greatest value we can."],["Boy","......"],["Cassha","Daniel, focus on what you can do. Grow at your own pace, and you'll be able to achieve more, better things."],["","Cassha gently brushes his cheek."],["Cassha","The battlefield's no place for you right now. But I know how much this means to you. We'll be waiting for you when you're ready."],["Boy","Cassha..."],["","Daniel keeps his lips tightly shut, his eyes gradually turning red."],["Arthur","Alright, kid, let's get you back. Don't get into trouble, okay? Cassha's been so busy she barely has a moment to herself, and today she even spent all that time talking with you... You'd better take it to heart."],["Boy","..."],["","Arthur takes Daniel's hand and leads him away, returning a few minutes later."],["Arthur","I had Selena take him back. She's reliable, so you don't need to worry, Cassha."],["Cassha","Okay. And Blazetrudge? How is he?"],["Arthur","He's been acting up. He's so strong we couldn't calm him down. In the end, we had to use a few doses of sedatives."],["Arthur","He's such a big guy that we had to use quite a bit... It's kind of sad to see."],["Cassha","Heh, you..."],["Cassha","Blazetrudge and... Mirestomp, both of them showed up very close to our base. Maybe we should consider pulling out."],["Arthur","You think our position's been compromised? Cassha, could it... could it be those guys again?"],["Cassha","......"],["Cassha","No, they no longer have any reason to oppose us now."],["Arthur","..."],["","Arthur doesn't respond, her expression darkening. Cassha can tell she's lost in those memories again..."],["Cassha","What's wrong, little Arthur? We're going to be on the move again—aren't you happy?"],["Cassha","After we move, you'll have a big room filled with all the ST parts you want."],["","Arthur tries to pout, but can't hold back a small smile."],["Arthur","I'm not a kid anymore, Cassha. Don't... tease me like that."],["Cassha","Well, it worked, didn't it?"],["Arthur","Sigh... Alright. When Lorenzo gets back, we'll talk about it."],["Vesper Warrior","Sorry to interrupt, Captains. The patrol has detected something unusual. A group of mercenaries is approaching the outpost."],["Arthur","Again?! What's going on?"],["Vesper Warrior","N-not sure. They have a large formation and a clear target. It's very likely they're specifically coming for us."],["Cassha","There's no time to lose. Arthur, get the team ready. We need to deal with them on the spot and keep them from getting any closer!"],["Arthur","Got it!"],["Arthur","Arthur here. We've reached the target location."],["Arthur","The enemy is within attack range, requesting—wait, is that... Hades?!"],["Cassha","...It's that big guy, no doubt."],["Arthur","Who exactly are these mercenaries?"],["Cassha","Based on the intel we gathered earlier, he's likely the mastermind behind the attack on Sankara—"],["Douglas","Ha! Vesper! I knew you'd show up!"],["","The Hades advances slowly to the center of the battlefield. It stands exposed to every gun on the field, yet it shows no sign of backing down."],["Cassha","Sounds like you came here just for us. Is there some bad blood between us I don't know about?"],["Douglas","Bad blood? No, no, no. You're just a pack of strays. And you don't need a grudge to put down a stray, do you?"],["Vesper Warrior","Bastard! What the hell are you saying?! We are Vesper! We once—"],["Douglas","Used to? Are you still living in some dream of the past? Heh. Wake up. This island doesn't care how glorious you used to be—"],["Douglas","All it'll tell you is that when it's your time to go, you stop struggling. At best, you give whatever's left of you to someone else."],["Vesper Warrior","You—!"],["Arthur","Enough talk! You're pretty cocky. Looks like you won't learn your place until someone teaches you a hard lesson!"],["Douglas","Remember my name, girlie. I'm Douglas. Soon everything you have will be mine, and then I'll turn this godforsaken island upside down!"],["Cassha","Is that so? Then give it a try..."],["Cassha","Assault squad, move out!"]],"468397301":[["Arthur","Come on... come on... COME ON!"],["","Arthur slams the missile launch button. Flames erupt from her Igniter's shoulders as the shells shoot like blades toward the Hades in midair."],["Arthur","!?"],["Arthur","We've got him! He's going down—move in and finish him!"],["","The Hades's engine is still running when it hits the ground. The force of the impact sends it skidding along, and any ST that tries to close in is knocked flying."],["Cassha","Spread out! Long-range suppression!"],["Vesper Warrior","Oh no! Captain, there's a gap over there! He's trying to break through!"],["","Cassha gives chase. Her rounds trace the Hades's path, burying themselves deep in the concrete."],["Cassha","Is that all you've got, Douglas?"],["","The Hades charges on through the storm of gunfire. In the cockpit, Douglas is drenched in sweat. The salt seeps into his unhealed wounds again, but he doesn't even notice."],["Cassha","How does it feel to be hunted by a pack of strays? Has that woken you up from your sweet little dream?"],["Douglas","Shut up! Shut up! I won't lose! Die, you damn woman!"],["","The blue glow of a railgun lights up on the Hades's back. Cassha's expression hardens."],["Cassha","Watch out—evade!"],["","BOOM! A chain of explosions rings out. Cassha is taken aback as she feels a powerful tremor. At the last second, the Hades has shifted its aim and blasted through the building beside her."],["Arthur","Cassha! I'm picking up explosives!"],["","FierceJaw quickly falls back, and a second later, the spot where it was standing is engulfed in flames."],["Arthur","Cassha, are you okay?!"],["Cassha","Ugh... I'm fine, just... a bit shaken."],["Vesper Warrior","Captain! Douglas is getting away—we've got to chase him!"],["Arthur","No. We can't leave the wounded behind."],["Vesper Warrior","Then let me! I'll go!"],["Arthur","No! Dasko, even with the Hades in bad shape, chasing him with what we've got left is too big a gamble. Let alone going after him alone."],["Vesper Warrior","So we just stand here and let Douglas escape?!"],["Vesper Warrior","Some nobody from who knows where humiliates us like that... and we're really just going to take it?!"],["Cassha","...Dasko, Arthur is right. The priority is to treat the injured."],["Vesper Warrior","Captain Cassha!"],["Cassha","Douglas is just a petty opportunist picking through the wreckage. Throwing away our comrades' lives just to take his? I don't remember Vesper ever working that way."],["Vesper Warrior","Captain..."],["Cassha","Calm down, Dasko. We need to move fast."],["","Cassha pauses and gazes off in the direction the Hades fled, a thoughtful look on her face."],["Vesper Warrior","Don't be upset, Daniel. You'll be home soon. Your family and friends will be waiting for you."],["Boy","......"],["Boy","Yeah. I know all the roads around here."],["","He's getting closer to home, but at the same time, farther away."],["Vesper Warrior","Still feeling down? Look, Daniel, the captains are just looking out for you. Being in Vesper... it's quite dangerous right now."],["Boy","I know. But isn't everywhere dangerous these days?"],["Vesper Warrior","...You're pretty sharp for your age."],["","Selena's soft laugh crackles over the communication channel."],["Vesper Warrior","But if it's danger we can see coming, danger we can help you avoid, then of course we'll step in."],["Vesper Warrior","That's why the captains want you to go home."],["Boy","..."],["Vesper Warrior","Uh—so, speaking of home, what do you like to do back there, Daniel?"],["Boy","..."],["Boy","My dad... he taught me to pilot STs."],["Vesper Warrior","No wonder you're so good at piloting STs. So you learned from your dad."],["","Daniel opens his mouth to say more, but before he can, his eyes well up."],["Vesper Warrior","Anything else? Like playing games with friends? Or, hmm... Oh! Eating a big meal with everyone!"],["Boy","..."],["Boy","We... we all go... to see the flowers Lorna planted... together."],["Vesper Warrior","Flowers? In Sankara? That's quite rare!"],["Boy","Yes, Lorna did it. She worked so hard to grow them."],["Vesper Warrior","That sounds nice. I haven't seen flowers in a long time... heh. Only the kind that burst from a gun barrel."],["Boy","......"],["Vesper Warrior","See? There are still plenty of good things waiting for you back home."],["Boy","That's not what I want to do—"],["Vesper Warrior","Then do you know why we're doing all this?"],["Boy","I..."],["Vesper Warrior","It's for you—for all of you. So that you, and us, all of us... can live safely and happily, doing those little things you just talked about."],["Boy","..."],["Vesper Warrior","...Too bad a life like that still feels so far away. Heh... Daniel, what is it you really want?"],["Vesper Warrior","You're so set on joining Vesper... What's driving you?"],["Boy","I... I'm doing it for... my... my—"],["","Beep beep—beep beep beep—"],["Cassha","Selena? Daniel? How're you guys doing out there?"],["Vesper Warrior","Captain? We're all good. What's up?"],["Cassha","We just encountered a mercenary ambush—"],["","Daniel suddenly shudders violently."],["Cassha","Their leader's a guy called Douglas. He escaped in the Hades."],["Boy","Ha... Hades...?!"],["Cassha","...That's right, Daniel. As you might've already guessed—he's one of the people who attacked you."],["","Daniel takes a deep breath, his mind gradually going blank."],["Cassha","The direction he escaped in is very troubling. I made a route analysis map. Try to take a detour and avoid confronting him."],["","A map full of markers appears on Daniel's screen."],["Cassha","Remember, report to me first if anything seems off. I've arranged for Arthur to control the situation here, so she can support you at any time."],["Cassha","You won't be bothering me, okay?"],["Vesper Warrior","I understand, Captain. I'll be careful and protect—Daniel?! Where are you going?!!"],["","The Aker suddenly swerves, speeding up as it veers off course."],["Cassha","What's going on?"],["Vesper Warrior","Captain, something's wrong. Daniel suddenly changed his route. He's heading to where Douglas might be!"],["Cassha","What?! Stop him—now. Selena, keep your coordinates synced in real time. I'm heading there."],["","Daniel is going faster than he's ever gone in his life. The rough terrain jolts him so hard it feels like his whole body might fall apart."],["","But he can't control the excitement surging inside him—or is it hatred?"],["","That overwhelming emotion drives him onward, closer and closer to the bastard who killed every hope he had."],["Vesper Warrior","Daniel, stop! It's too dangerous up ahead! You'll get yourself killed!"],["Boy","Dying isn't that scary, Selena. Dad's already dead. I'll just be getting closer to him—I'm going to avenge him!"],["Vesper Warrior","Avenge him? Your dad? Wait, you don't mean—"],["Boy","I'm the one who saved him. I'm the one who let him hurt everyone... and kill Dad. I'll take responsibility for all of it..."],["Vesper Warrior","—?! You're going to take on the Hades by yourself?! Are you crazy?! Daniel! You have to calm down!"],["Boy","I know it's dangerous, Selena, so don't follow me. What I'm about to do has nothing to do with you—"],["Vesper Warrior","Nonsense! I promised the captain I'd get you home safe! Stop and let's talk! Your dad—your dad would want you to live!"],["Boy","..."],["","It's as if someone has dumped a bucket of cold water over Daniel. A faint glimmer of reason slowly creeps back into his mind."],["","That's right... Right up until the end, Dad fought to keep him alive."],["","The Aker gradually slows. Daniel's mind is torn in two, and his hands are shaking so hard he can barely hold the control stick."],["Boy","But... Selena... I wanted... I wanted Dad to live too..."],["","RUMBLE—A tremor suddenly rolls toward them from the distance. Daniel turns to the side, confused."],["","Trees are ripped out of the ground one after another, hurled aside as the Hades's battered, massive frame storms in, wrapped in a howling gale—"],["Boy","—!!"],["Boy","Selena, look out! Stay back!!"],["Douglas","Bzz—bzz—"],["Douglas","—What's in my way?"],["Boy","...Gutzman?! Is it really you—"],["Douglas","Gutzman? Gutzman's dead, isn't he? No... no, I never saw the body. Maybe that bastard's still alive!"],["Boy","What are you talking about? Aren't you Gutzman?"],["Douglas","Bullshit! I'm Douglas! The one and only Douglas!"],["Boy","Douglas...?"],["Douglas","Who are you again? I've heard your voice—yes, just recently, I've heard your voice, you are..."],["Boy","Daniel, I'm Daniel, the one who dug you out from under the rock!"],["Douglas","Daniel... Daniel... oh, it's you. What are you doing out here in an ST? Come to bring me food or something?"],["Boy","...? You killed my dad... how can you feel nothing? How can you talk to me like nothing happened?"],["Douglas","Heh... what are you saying, kid? You saved me—kept me alive. That's my fate. The life Douglas was meant to have."],["Douglas","As for your father dying by my hand—that was his fate too. You should be glad he died early. A hellhole like Milkhama was never a place for people like you..."],["Douglas","Too bad you're still alive. Does it hurt? Want me to send you to join him—"],["Vesper Warrior","Daniel!"],["","Selena fires two grappling lines, locking onto the Aker and pulling it back—but the Hades instantly shifts its aim. A burst of gunfire rips out, all of it redirected toward Selena."],["Vesper Warrior","Ugh—!"],["","The force of the impact knocks both Selena's and Daniel's STs to the ground. Even with Selena's ST cushioning the blow, Daniel's head still slams hard against the seat back, sending a sharp pain through his skull."],["Vesper Warrior","Da-Daniel, are you... okay?"],["Boy","Selena...? I..."],["Vesper Warrior","I... sent a distress signal... don't—don't worry..."],["","Selena's voice gradually fades away."],["","Daniel's mind goes completely blank, a wave of dizziness and nausea crashing over him. But somewhere deep down, he still knows—there's something important he has to do... something he absolutely can't forget."],["","The Hades slowly approaches the two downed STs."],["Douglas","Just the two of you... and you thought you could kill me? Gotta admire the guts."],["","The Hades raises its gun again."],["Douglas","I already spared your life once, kid. For whatever damn reason—I let you live."],["Douglas","You won't survive on this island. Might as well end it now and save you the suffering later."],["Douglas","Heh... heh heh... no need to thank me—"],["","Bang!"],["","A bullet strikes the Hades's hull, leaving only a shallow dent."],["Douglas","...?"],["Boy","I... won't..."],["","Bang! Bang! Two bullets hit the Hades's shell, scattering a few sparks."],["Boy","...let you..."],["","The Aker props itself up and keeps firing at the Hades, but each shot only leaves a shallow dent on the Hades's shell."],["Boy","...hurt... any..."],["Douglas","...Hmph."],["Douglas","I hear the defiance, kid. If you still remember this in your next life... you're welcome to come try and kill me again."],["","With the Hades's gun trained on it, the Aker slowly rises to its feet, shielding the ST behind it completely, and raises its gun once more."],["Boy","I won't... let you... hurt... anyone... ever again..."],["Douglas","...Looks like that crash scrambled your brain, Daniel. But it doesn't matter—soon, you'll be free of it all!"],["","The Hades slowly squeezes the trigger—just as the Aker takes a step forward."],["Boy","Raaaaaaaagh!!!"],["","*BOOM——*"],["","The next second, a dazzling blue electromagnetic beam shoots past the Aker from behind. The Hades's weapon melts on the spot, and the sheer force of the blast hurls its frame backward!"],["Douglas","Who?!"],["","Kzzzt—kzzzt—"],["","I really don't like this kind of ending."],["","The Hades's targeting system quickly locks onto the threat: a red dot closing in at high speed—"],["","It's just one of them! Just one!"],["","Douglas grits his teeth, maxes out the engine's power output, and rams the approaching Dias."],["","Libby—"],["Libby","I am no longer needed now, Miss Mirestomp..."],["","Mirestomp freezes for a split second, then pulls the trigger on instinct—and at the same moment, an even fiercer barrage erupts from behind the Hades. Caught in the crossfire, the Hades begins to crack and shatter under the searing blast, piece by piece."],["Douglas","Ugh—! Damn it—damn it—! I won't lose! I haven't—lost—!!"],["Douglas","GAAAAAAAGHHH—!"],["","BOOM! The Hades's cockpit blows apart. The massive machine comes crashing down, shards of steel stabbing into the earth like swords, flames raging everywhere."],["","In the Dias, Mirestomp watches the dual-wielding FierceJaw in the distance and takes a step forward."],["Mirestomp","...Captain Cassha."],["Cassha","Snow."],["","Before either of them can say more, a dull thud reaches their ears."],["","—The Aker has collapsed."],["","Daniel dreams again—dreams of the past."],["","Every memory of his father swirls through his mind. In every timeline, he hears his father calling his name and sees himself running toward him."],["","In every timeline, they're together, walking happily off into the distance. Only now, in this moment, does Daniel understand—those scenes will never happen again. His dad is never coming back..."],["","I'm so glad you're both alive."],["","He feels someone wiping away his tears. Their hand is dry and warm, and he wants to open his eyes and see who it is."],["","It's all over, Daniel. No more worrying... no more being afraid..."],["Boy","...Cassha...?"],["Cassha","Yes, it's me. You're safe now."],["Boy","Dou...glas...?"],["Cassha","He's dead."],["Boy","..."],["Boy","What about Selena..."],["Cassha","She's unconscious, but it's okay. The medical team will be here soon."],["Boy","...Thank... goodness."],["Cassha","..."],["Cassha","......"],["Cassha","So Douglas was the reason you were so set on joining Vesper?"],["Boy","...Yeah. He killed Dad... Dad's blood... it kept pouring out of the wound, and no matter what I did, I couldn't wipe it away... and then he couldn't hear me anymore."],["Boy","But, but I'm the one who brought him back to camp, Cassha. It was me, it was all me..."],["Boy","It was me... I was naive... I thought if people just tried to understand each other... things would get better... I..."],["","Cassha gently touches his face."],["Cassha","In Milkhama, being a good person takes a lot of courage and strength, because the bad people here are just too strong."],["Cassha","But if, even somewhere this hard, we still blame someone for trying to be good, the bad people will only grow in number and strength. Milkhama will become worse than hell, and our dream will never come true."],["Boy","Because... I'm not strong enough? So my kindness... might get even more people killed..."],["Cassha","No one's born strong, Daniel. Don't blame yourself for being weak, and don't let it make you throw away who you are."],["Cassha","If we surrender to evil from the very start, what will we have left to hold on to?"],["Boy","...But Dad's dead, Cassha. What... what am I supposed to do now? My future... where is it..."],["Cassha","...You've already found the courage to face death, Daniel. So live—take that same courage and use it to face the life ahead of you. Don't give up, not until you..."],["Cassha","...become the person you've always wanted to be."],["Boy","...Can I... still do that?"],["Cassha","Of course you can. Anyone can. Now sleep. You can rest now. When you wake up, it'll be a fresh start."],["Boy","................"],["Mirestomp","Captain Cassha's still as gentle as ever... not that I'm surprised."],["","Cassha looks up and sees Mirestomp watching her with a smile from a safe distance—and she knows that, on the high ground farther off, another ST is watching everything."],["Mirestomp","Why not try being a little gentle with yourself for once?"],["Cassha","I heard, Snow. You paid a visit to Vesper's base."],["Mirestomp","...Yes."],["Cassha","Heh. Hard to find, wasn't it? Did you have to pull a lot of strings?"],["Mirestomp","Not really. I just happened to be passing by. I figured things probably weren't going too well for you these days, so I dropped by to watch the show."],["Cassha","See anything?"],["Mirestomp","You don't seem to have a clear grasp of your situation, Captain Cassha. What I saw was a pack of strays anyone could kick around—"],["Mirestomp","Like that guy who just died—Douglas, was it? Heh. Even someone like that has the nerve to come after you now. I'd say things are only going to get harder for you from here, wouldn't you?"],["Cassha","Heh."],["Cassha","Yes. We've lost an important leader. We've got enemies on every side, and we're on our own. So now more than ever, we'll stay sharp, avoid unnecessary fights, and protect the comrades we have left."],["Mirestomp","......"],["Mirestomp","..."],["Mirestomp","Wouldn't one more gun to help protect them... be a good thing?"],["","For once, Mirestomp actually says it. The smile on her face doesn't change in the slightest, but this might be the only time she's ever shown any weakness—and the furthest she's ever gone."],["","Cassha pauses for a moment, then a faint smile tugs at her lips."],["Cassha","Ah... so that's it, Snow. That's why you really came."],["Mirestomp","...What on earth are you talking about, Captain?"],["","Mirestomp's guard goes right back up."],["Cassha","The reason we turned Goman down... I doubt he told you, did he? I could tell you myself—"],["Mirestomp","No need. I don't care what you all think. It's the same old song and dance."],["Cassha","......"],["Mirestomp","Besides your kindness... your stubbornness hasn't changed either, Captain."],["Cassha","Hehe..."],["Cassha","Snow, don't let what happened to Vesper become a weight you carry. We've gone our separate ways. If you believe in your choice, then you've accepted whatever future it brings—and so have we."],["Mirestomp","...Even if you're just waiting to die?"],["Cassha","Why assume the worst from the start? As long as we're alive, there's always a chance to create something more. I trust my teammates—just as they trust me."],["Cassha","No one's waiting to die. We're still fighting to carry on the ideals and hopes we all shared... Phoenix is gone, and that can't be changed, but we'll carry on his fight to the very end."],["Mirestomp","..."],["Mirestomp","Hah... Looks like there's no show to watch this time either."],["Cassha","Heh. Go home with your friend."],["Mirestomp","She's not my \"friend.\""],["","Cassha glances distantly at Aglow, stationed on the high ground."],["Cassha","I didn't mean her. Blazetrudge—he got separated from you. He's at our base now."],["Mirestomp","—?!"],["Cassha","I'll tell Arthur so you can go pick him up—"],["","Cassha smiles slightly."],["Cassha","And after that, don't look back."],["Vesper Warrior","Heh... the sun feels nice. Makes the wound itch."],["Vesper Warrior","Itching means it's healing. Stop moving around."],["Vesper Warrior","I'm being good, Dasko. I didn't even reach out to comfort Daniel when he came crying to say goodbye."],["Vesper Warrior","......"],["","Dasko doesn't answer. Selena glances up at him. The kid is sitting on the ground hugging his knees, lost in thought."],["Vesper Warrior","You've had something on your mind ever since we got back. What, did something happen while I was out cold?"],["Vesper Warrior","Nothing..."],["Vesper Warrior","If it's nothing, why'd you look away? That means it's something."],["Vesper Warrior","...I just think you didn't have to get hurt. If Captain Cassha had let us split up and go after Douglas, you never would've run into this mess!"],["Vesper Warrior","And you wouldn't... have ended up like this."],["Vesper Warrior","The captain couldn't have seen this coming. Besides, Captain Cassha did everything she could to keep everyone safe..."],["Vesper Warrior","Don't you think the captain's really... really... oh, you know what I mean!"],["Vesper Warrior","......"],["Vesper Warrior","Dasko, I don't know what you guys say behind closed doors, but I really hope you understand: Captain Cassha—and every other captain—they're all incredible soldiers."],["Vesper Warrior","Soldiers... heh... If they were really such incredible soldiers, we wouldn't be here right now."],["Vesper Warrior","And where does that leave us? In Lukmund's private prison? A DL military court?"],["Vesper Warrior","Why do you always talk us down? Are we just doomed to lose? If we find a way to deal with Lukmund, if we take out the one who got Phoenix killed, we can take back the upper hand and be the Vesper we used to be!"],["Vesper Warrior","...Dasko, none of us can accept Phoenix's death. But that's no reason to turn our blades on Lukmund right now—"],["Vesper Warrior","Why not? If we just kill Lukmund—!"],["Vesper Warrior","Will Phoenix come back and lead us again?"],["Vesper Warrior","......"],["Vesper Warrior","..."],["Vesper Warrior","...No, he won't, Selena. Phoenix is gone... What... what are we supposed to do now? Where's our future...?"],["Vesper Warrior","Dasko..."],["Vesper Warrior","But at least... at least we can't just do nothing. While we've still got lives to put on the line, we should at least get justice for Phoenix, shouldn't we?!"],["Vesper Warrior","You really—cough! Cough, cough!"],["Vesper Warrior","Why are you coughing again? Fine, I'll shut up. Just enjoy the sun. I'll go get the medical team."],["Vesper Warrior","Das—cough!"],["","Dasko is gone in a flash. Selena lies on the stretcher, trying to call after him, but she can't stop coughing."],["","A bad feeling takes root in her heart, but she might not have the strength to stop things from heading that way. Is this another fate they can't escape?"],["","......"],["","After a while, she feels a little better. She can't see the sun in the clear blue sky, but its light still keeps her warm, and the gloom in her heart slowly begins to settle."],["","But... as long as the captains are still here... they'll get through anything. They will..."],["","Under the same sky, Libby gazes at Vesper's base in the distance."],["Libby","Your colors have gotten much \"quieter,\" Mirestomp."],["","Mirestomp is packing her backpack while Blazetrudge hands her things."],["Mirestomp","Is that so? You seem to have forgotten again—don't try to understand everything about me."],["Blazetrudge","Heh... heh... Mirestomp... doesn't like... people. Likes... Thunderbolt—"],["Mirestomp","Enough out of you, Blazetrudge. I haven't even settled things with you over this mess yet."],["Blazetrudge","...Blazetrudge... protect... Mirestomp."],["Mirestomp","...Sigh."],["Libby","It's getting late, you two."],["Mirestomp","......"],["","Mirestomp starts thinking about how to get Blazetrudge back. His ST is a total write-off, and borrowing one from Vesper is out of the question."],["Blazetrudge","Blazetrudge... run... home."],["","Mirestomp's lips curl into a smile."],["Mirestomp","...What, you think you're some kind of puppy?"],["Mirestomp","Come on. The Dias's cockpit can't fit you, but luckily its hand can just about hold you..."],["","The two of them head toward the Dias together, while Libby watches from not far away. In a field of vision she can share with no one, Libby sees two colors, pure and intense."],["","She thoughtfully touches her eyepatch, then quickly follows."]]};
